    src/lib/services/remote/remote_audio_player.dart
    src/lib/services/remote/remote_audio_sink.dart
    src/lib/services/remote/remote_mic_sender.dart
    src/lib/services/remote/remote_audit.dart
    src/lib/services/remote/remote_client_address.dart
    src/lib/services/db/remote_audit_dao.dart
    src/test/remote_*_test.dart (13 test files)

  Modified (additive; existing behaviour preserved):
    src/lib/services/data_broker.dart      remote peer + remote host transports
    src/lib/services/db/app_database_io.dart   new DAO, schema version 3 -> 4
    src/lib/services/db/app_database_stub.dart matching web stub getter
    src/lib/radio/pcm_player.dart          multicast playback tap
    src/lib/main.dart                      startup wiring for the remote role
    src/lib/dialogs/settings_dialog.dart   Remote Control settings section

Where this fork and the upstream differ in behaviour, the difference is
opt-in: with the remote role left at its default (Off), the application
behaves as upstream does.

